From 15995e8a8381188b1a0f7ed95e62398e98c6ba66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:59:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 174/181] gsplat: SplatEmit and BeautyNoSplatEmit, the splats'
 direct emission apart

Two render var sources for compositing:
- gsplat_emission: the composited splats' emission seen straight from
  the camera (no surface bounce yet, as Emission counts it), without the
  other emitters, lights or background. A colour AOV pass the film finds
  by name (KernelFilm.pass_gsplat_emission).
- combined_without_gsplat_emission: the beauty without it, in one layer.
With the pass on, the kernel writes that emission to it instead of the
beauty, so the denoiser works on everything else; the output driver adds
it back to every other read of the beauty. The beauty keeps the splats'
detail undenoised, the rest is denoised, and none goes negative (a first
version subtracted from the denoised beauty: -0.32 at splat edges).
A production frame, GPU, OIDN: C = BeautyNoSplatEmit + SplatEmit to half
precision, SplatEmit = Emit (splats are its only emitters), minimum 1e-4;
a scene with lights and an emissive mesh, no splats: SplatEmit 0,
BeautyNoSplatEmit = C. Toggles in the Cycles AOVs and Cycles Render
Settings LOPs (Light, Gaussian Splats). KernelFilm grows by 16 bytes:
a Houdini started on an older build must restart before a GPU render.
